# Workstation Toolchain Audit

Verify a personal fleet of self-built tools, daemons, and configs is actually
runnable — not merely present — and repair what is not. Built for the case where
a set of repos must be re-verified after a machine rebuild, an account change,
or a long gap: the code survived in git while the machine-specific assumptions
it encodes did not.

**Core principle:** a tool that exists, parses, and is wired up is not a working
tool. Every claim of "works" needs an executed command behind it.

`requesting-code-review` covers one repo's uncommitted diff. This covers a
fleet: installability, runtime, and whether the repo matches the live system.

